  "text" : "So two proposals go out as pull requests on a branch signed.\nMain is untouched.\nEach one carries the same version cross-check gate your own CI runs.\nSo a human reviewer sees exactly what would break before they approve anything.\nNothing here has a merge function, not a lockdown one, none at all.\nThe agent physically cannot ship its own change.\nLet me show you what this looks like when something actually happens.\nThis headline lands on a Tuesday.\nChina confirms a major discovery of low-contaminant niobium.\nAnd if you know that, niobium is the superconductor most quantum computers are built out of.\nThat headline should worry you because a quantum computer that breaks today's encryption is the single largest tail risk sitting on our books."
